{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>For you will serve their gods, for it will be a snare to you</b>. These instances of כי function in the sense of אשר, as in several places, and this is the meaning of 'אי,' which is one of the four usages that כי serves, as we find in several places, and this carries the conditional sense in the meaning of אשר, etc. — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 23:33). But it is not so. Rather, the reading of the verse is: <b>They shall not dwell in your land, for it will be a snare to you, lest they cause you to sin against Me, for you will serve their gods</b>. And thus He said (Exodus 23:32), \"Lest you make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land, lest it become a snare in your midst,\" and the reason is that their dwelling in your land will be a snare and a stumbling block to you — <b>lest they cause you to sin against Me</b> through their evil ways and their corrupt practices — <b>for you will serve their gods</b>, for they will entice you and lead you astray through this:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Rashi's comment as quoted here appears garbled in the Hebrew text; the reference to 'אי' and the four usages of כי does not correspond to Rashi's actual commentary on this verse, and the translation follows the Hebrew as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:15:20.157044047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}